  "finding_four_dcs_never_writes_a_long_vocalic_liquid": {
    "claim": "Across the 534 DCS files fetched here, 1,651 distinct verb lemmas, not one contains a long vocalic r or l.",
    "measured": {
      "lemmas_with_long_vocalic_r_or_l": 0,
      "distinct_verb_lemmas": 1651,
      "examples": {
        "stṛ": 17,
        "stṝ": 0,
        "kṛ": 706,
        "kṝ": 0,
        "tṛ": 45,
        "tṝ": 0,
        "gṛ": 21,
        "gṝ": 0
      }
    },
    "consequence": "DCS's spelling cannot distinguish two roots the Rigvedic map gives OPPOSITE predicates: str̥- lays low (DESTROYS) and str̥̄- strews the sacred grass (ESTABLISHES). This has the same shape as the root_folded hazard the root map itself names -- a key that looks unambiguous and is not -- and it produced a real defect before it was found. DCS resolution now runs over a length-neutral bucket."
  }
